    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53594" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κασῆς</span></b> , ὁ (on the
		accent v. Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
			1.63
		</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>skin</i> used as a
				<i>saddle</i> or <i>horse-cloth</i>, acc. sg. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κασᾶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					8.3.8
				</span></i>
			; acc. dual <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κασᾶ</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				8.3.7
			</span></i>; acc. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κασᾶς</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				8.3.6
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλέσας</span> codd.), <i><span class="en">
				Agatharch.
				20
			</span></i>; nom. sg. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κασῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PTeb.</u>
					38.22
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii B. C.)</span>; abbreviated in <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLond.</u>
				2.402v5
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>: written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κασσ-</span> by <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				7.68
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάσσος, κασσοποιός</span>.
			(Ethiopian word, <i><span class="en">
				Agatharch.
			</span></i> l. c.; cf. Hebr. <i>kāsāh</i>
			'covered'.)</div>
